00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:12.311
which is kind of like a hot dog,

00:10:12.311 --> 00:10:14.280
but with a Cumberland-style sausage,

00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:16.215
which is something that's kind
of popular here in the UK.

00:10:16.215 --> 00:10:18.284
But, unfortunately, due to
the reduced pandemic menu,

00:10:18.284 --> 00:10:19.919
we weren't able to get these.

00:10:19.919 --> 00:10:22.121
Joe: Harry, you know my
feelings about the hot dogs,

00:10:22.121 --> 00:10:23.856
you know my feelings
about hot dogs in general,

00:10:23.856 --> 00:10:25.424
and I will say, as someone who was

00:10:25.424 --> 00:10:27.827
born and raised in "Shack-cago,"

00:10:27.827 --> 00:10:31.430
I would love to try the Shack-cago hot dog

00:10:31.430 --> 00:10:32.498
at the UK Shake Shack.

00:10:32.498 --> 00:10:35.234
So, when I come to visit,
that'll be our first stop.

00:10:35.368 --> 00:10:36.802
Harry: Now, on top of 
the limited-edition

00:10:36.802 --> 00:10:37.637
hot chicken burger,

00:10:37.637 --> 00:10:40.706
we can also currently get
some hot chicken bites,

00:10:40.706 --> 00:10:43.242
as well as some spicy fries.

00:10:43.242 --> 00:10:44.543
Joe: So, the only two sandwiches

00:10:44.543 --> 00:10:45.978
that we were able to get our hands on

00:10:45.978 --> 00:10:47.079
that are exclusive to the US

00:10:47.079 --> 00:10:49.148
and not in the UK are the grilled cheese

00:10:49.148 --> 00:10:51.484
and the Korean chicken sandwich.

00:10:51.484 --> 00:10:54.754
OK, first things first,
this grilled cheese.

00:10:54.954 --> 00:10:56.055
Look at this thing!

00:10:56.055 --> 00:10:59.525
Did you, is it, do you sit on this, too?

00:10:59.525 --> 00:11:01.327
This is ridiculous!

00:11:01.327 --> 00:11:03.696
I wouldn't pay a dollar for this.

00:11:03.696 --> 00:11:05.331
It looks like they took two buns,

00:11:05.331 --> 00:11:07.366
put cheese in it, and then, I don't know,

00:11:07.366 --> 00:11:09.402
ran over it with a
steamroller or something.

00:11:09.402 --> 00:11:11.137
Why is this so thin?

00:11:11.137 --> 00:11:13.005
What does look actually

00:11:13.005 --> 00:11:14.040
♪ bomb ♪

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:17.443
is this, the Korean chicken sandwich.

00:11:20.646 --> 00:11:22.682
Yo. Yes!

00:11:22.682 --> 00:11:23.949
Yes to this.

00:11:23.949 --> 00:11:25.351
Oh, my goodness.

00:11:25.351 --> 00:11:26.585
With the kimchi.

00:11:26.585 --> 00:11:28.254
I'm telling you, I'm telling you.

00:11:30.289 --> 00:11:31.824
You want that.

00:11:31.824 --> 00:11:33.292
Also a thing the Shake Shack in the US has

00:11:33.292 --> 00:11:34.193
that you can't get in the UK

00:11:34.193 --> 00:11:35.494
are the breakfast sandwiches.

00:11:35.494 --> 00:11:37.396
We're shooting this, like, at 4 p.m.,

00:11:37.396 --> 00:11:38.731
so surprise to no one,

00:11:38.731 --> 00:11:40.466
the breakfast sandwiches
were not available.

00:11:40.466 --> 00:11:41.834
But, usually, if you get there

00:11:41.834 --> 00:11:43.436
I'm assuming before 10:30 or 11,

00:11:43.436 --> 00:11:44.804
you can get a bacon, egg, and cheese;

00:11:44.804 --> 00:11:46.205
sausage, egg, and cheese;

00:11:46.205 --> 00:11:47.339
and just an egg and cheese.

00:11:47.339 --> 00:11:48.174
Check 'em out.

00:11:49.508 --> 00:11:51.310
I have no idea if they taste good or not.

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:51.343
Also a thing you can get in the US

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:54.480
Also a thing you can get in the US

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:57.450
is cheesy bacon fries.

00:11:57.450 --> 00:11:59.852
But this has been sitting
for more than a minute.

00:11:59.852 --> 00:11:59.919
Oh, my God, I think it's
gonna come out like a disk!

00:11:59.952 --> 00:12:02.054
Oh, my God, I think it's
gonna come out like a disk!

00:12:02.054 --> 00:12:04.757
[laughs] Oh, God!

00:12:04.757 --> 00:12:06.192
I wanna make this perfectly clear:

00:12:06.192 --> 00:12:09.729
This is not an indictment
of Shake Shack quality.

00:12:09.729 --> 00:12:12.098
This has been sitting for,
what, at least two hours?

00:12:12.098 --> 00:12:14.033
I mean, it's bacon and cheese on fries.

00:12:15.234 --> 00:12:17.403
Even at that consistency,
it's still pretty good.

00:12:17.403 --> 00:12:19.538
I mentioned this before,
but there's, like,

00:12:19.538 --> 00:12:22.441
all these different regional
things throughout the country,

00:12:22.441 --> 00:12:24.543
so I don't know if this
whole Korean sandwich

00:12:24.543 --> 00:12:29.248
and Korean chicken bites
is just in this area.

00:12:29.248 --> 00:12:33.753
But I think I'm about to lose my mind.

00:12:35.621 --> 00:12:38.190
Yo, you want this.

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:39.959
Oh, yes!

00:12:39.959 --> 00:12:40.893
Yes to these.

00:12:40.893 --> 00:12:42.428
Yes to these!

00:12:42.428 --> 00:12:44.196
Harry: Now, much like
the way US Shake Shacks

00:12:44.196 --> 00:12:46.132
have exclusive burgers and custards,

00:12:46.132 --> 00:12:47.633
some of the UK branches also have

00:12:47.633 --> 00:12:49.268
exclusive options themselves.

00:12:49.268 --> 00:12:51.036
The one we went to had a dessert option

00:12:51.036 --> 00:12:54.173
called the Union Shack, which
is a really terrible pun

00:12:54.173 --> 00:12:56.909
on the Union Jack, which is our flag.

00:12:56.909 --> 00:12:58.844
Now, it's effectively
just a chocolate custard

00:12:58.844 --> 00:13:01.247
with some chocolate from
British chocolatiers.

00:13:01.247 --> 00:13:02.915
However, unfortunately,
due to the pandemic,

00:13:02.915 --> 00:13:04.917
reduced menu, couldn't get that either.

00:13:04.917 --> 00:13:06.952
And, of course, it wouldn't
be a Shake Shack episode

00:13:06.952 --> 00:13:08.788
unless we talked about the shakes.

00:13:08.788 --> 00:13:10.790
Now, the UK-wide exclusive flavors

00:13:10.790 --> 00:13:13.159
include coffee and caramel,

00:13:13.159 --> 00:13:14.393
and then the branch we visited

00:13:14.393 --> 00:13:16.295
also had a cinnamon toast shake,

00:13:16.295 --> 00:13:17.496
which I'm really intrigued by.

00:13:19.031 --> 00:13:20.199
Mixy, mixy.

00:13:24.403 --> 00:13:25.738
It's not bad.

00:13:25.738 --> 00:13:27.907
Very sweet, and quite cinnamony,

00:13:27.907 --> 00:13:29.141
as you would expect.

00:13:30.342 --> 00:13:33.612
Joe: It's so many different
menu items across regions

00:13:33.612 --> 00:13:36.582
it'd be impossible for us
to cover all the things

00:13:36.582 --> 00:13:39.151
at every specific Shake
Shack in the US alone,

00:13:39.151 --> 00:13:42.021
so given the ones that
we had that we went to,

00:13:42.021 --> 00:13:45.157
the three exclusive shakes we have are

00:13:45.157 --> 00:13:46.959
brownie batter hot cocoa,

00:13:46.959 --> 00:13:49.862
vanilla black sugar, cookies and cream.

00:13:49.862 --> 00:13:53.299
Once again, end of the
day, end of the shoot.

00:13:53.299 --> 00:13:55.601
Gonna put me into a coma after this.

00:13:55.601 --> 00:13:57.236
Yeah, that's pretty good.

00:13:57.236 --> 00:13:58.637
Like, it has a little bit of, like,

00:13:58.637 --> 00:14:00.239
an extra chocolatyness to it.

00:14:01.974 --> 00:14:03.642
It's not too sweet.

00:14:03.642 --> 00:14:04.877
The caramel flavor is there,

00:14:04.877 --> 00:14:06.712
but it isn't, like, chemically tasting.

00:14:07.813 --> 00:14:08.948
That's the one to beat.

00:14:10.349 --> 00:14:11.951
Cookies and cream, baby.

00:14:11.951 --> 00:14:13.853
♪ Cookies and cream ♪

00:14:13.853 --> 00:14:14.820
Woop.

00:14:14.820 --> 00:14:15.654
There we go.

00:14:16.622 --> 00:14:18.490
I can't decide if that one's better.

00:14:18.490 --> 00:14:19.391
That's so good.

